  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Give reasons for the following:
(a) Venous blood is more acidic than arterial blood. (2 marks)
(b) Earthworms come out of their burrows during heavy rain. (1 mark)', '(a) Venous blood collects carbon dioxide produced by respiring tissues. In the red cells CO2 combines with water to form carbonic acid with the help of carbonic anhydrase, and this dissociates into H+ and bicarbonate ions. The extra H+ makes venous blood slightly more acidic (pH about 7.35) than arterial blood (about 7.4). (b) Earthworms respire through their moist skin using oxygen from the air in the soil. Heavy rain fills the burrows and soil spaces with water, so there is too little oxygen; they come out to the surface to breathe and avoid drowning.', null, '[{"point": "(a) Venous blood carries more CO2 from respiring tissues; CO2 + H2O → H2CO3 → H+ + HCO3- (carbonic anhydrase), raising H+ and lowering pH (about 7.35 vs 7.4)", "marks": 2}, {"point": "(b) Burrows fill with water, so the air (oxygen) in the soil is displaced; earthworms breathe through moist skin and come out to get oxygen (and avoid drowning)", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
