  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'There is greater biodiversity in tropical and sub-tropical regions than in temperate regions. Explain. (3 marks)', '(1) Evolutionary time: temperate regions were repeatedly covered by ice during the glaciations, while tropical regions stayed relatively undisturbed for millions of years, giving more time for speciation and diversification. (2) Stable environment: the tropics have a less seasonal, more constant and predictable climate, which encourages niche specialisation and allows many species to coexist. (3) Energy and productivity: tropical regions receive more solar energy and warmth, and often more rain, so productivity is higher, which supports more species and more complex food webs.', null, '[{"point": "Tropics were less affected by glaciations, so they had a long, undisturbed evolutionary time for speciation", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Stable, less seasonal climate with predictable conditions allows niche specialisation", "marks": 1}, {"point": "More solar energy, warmth and rainfall give higher productivity, supporting more species", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge') and t.slug = 'bio-science-general-subject-knowledge'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-2'), 'standard', 3,
