  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'The chemical equation below shows the hydrolysis of cane sugar in aqueous solution in the presence of mineral acid:
C12H22O11 + H2O + [H2SO4] →
(a) Complete the equation on the product side. What are the products formed? (2 marks)
(b) Of the three reactants in the equation, which acts as a catalyst? (1 mark)', '(a) C12H22O11 + H2O —(H2SO4)→ C6H12O6 + C6H12O6. The products are glucose and fructose (an equimolar mixture called invert sugar). (b) The sulphuric acid (its H+ ions) acts as the catalyst; it speeds up the reaction but is not used up. (Because water is in large excess, the reaction is pseudo-first order.)', null, '[{"point": "(a) C12H22O11 + H2O → C6H12O6 + C6H12O6 (with H2SO4 shown over the arrow)", "marks": 1}, {"point": "Products: glucose and fructose (invert sugar)", "marks": 1}, {"point": "(b) H2SO4 (the H+ of the mineral acid) is the catalyst", "marks": 1}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
