  values ('ME', 'short_answer', 'Explain the following terms with reference to the use of pesticides:
(a) Bioconcentration (1.5 marks)
(b) Biomagnification (1.5 marks)', '(a) Bioconcentration is the build-up of a chemical such as a pesticide inside an organism directly from its surroundings (water or soil), so that its concentration in the body becomes higher than in the environment - for example, fish absorbing DDT from water through their gills and storing it in fat. (b) Biomagnification is the increase in concentration of a persistent, non-biodegradable, fat-soluble pesticide at each higher trophic level of a food chain, because it is not broken down or excreted and each consumer eats many contaminated organisms - e.g. DDT rising from water to plankton to fish to fish-eating birds, causing thin eggshells and population decline in the top predators.', null, '[{"point": "(a) Bioconcentration: accumulation of a pesticide in an organism directly from the surrounding water/ environment to a concentration higher than outside (e.g. fish absorbing DDT through gills)", "marks": 1.5}, {"point": "(b) Biomagnification: increase in concentration of a persistent, non-biodegradable pesticide (e.g. DDT) at successive trophic levels of a food chain; top predators (fish-eating birds) worst affected - thin eggshells", "marks": 1.5}]'::jsonb, (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge'),
    (select t.id from public.topics t where t.subject_id = (select id from public.subjects where slug = 'general-subject-knowledge') and t.slug = 'bio-science-general-subject-knowledge'), (select id from public.exam_papers where code = 'me-technical-2'), 'standard', 3,
    324, 'historical_official', 'awaiting_review',
